  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)... \n\nKEY POINTS \n\n1. Coastal flooding and beach erosion from high tides 6.5 to 7 ft\nand elevated surf at times is expected through next week.\n\n2. Rain chances increase for Sunday through Tuesday across the \narea. Highest chances of rain are Sunday into Monday. We're \nmonitoring the potential for flash and urban flooding.\n\n3. There is a potential for increased winds from the coastal \nwaters to the deserts Sunday into Monday\n\nDISCUSSION \n\nThe cooling trend will continue into early next week, with high \ntemperatures falling to as much as 10 to 15 degrees below average\nfor the mountains, deserts, and inland valleys. High temperatures\nMonday through Wednesday will be mostly in the upper 60s to low \n70s for the coast and valleys, with the lower deserts in the \nlower to mid 80s. This will make for temperatures 20-30 degrees \ncooler than observed just a few days earlier during the heatwave.\n\nA low pressure system will absorb the moisture from what is left\nof former Hurricane Rachel, then move northeastward into extreme \nsouthern California and northern Baja. This will bring showers \nchances for Sunday through Tuesday with the greatest chances of \nrain Sunday into Monday. Rain totals for the whole event may as \nhigh as around 0.50 to 2.00 inches (highest in the mountains) for\nportions of the forecast area. There could be a few inches of \nsnowfall on the very highest mountain peaks above 9000 feet for \nMonday night and Tuesday as snow levels may briefly fall as low as\n8000 feet.\n\nOnshore winds will strengthen for Sunday and Monday with southwest\nto west winds for Sunday afternoon through Monday morning gusting\nto 20 to 30 mph for the coastal waters to the valleys and to 35 to\n45 mph for the mountains and deserts with gusts to 55 to 65 mph\nfor the northern Coachella Valley below the San Gorgonio Pass.\nThere is the potential for strong wind from the coastal waters to\nthe deserts Sunday into Monday. \n\nPlease continue to monitor the forecast for the dynamic impacts \ndue to remnants of Rachel.",
